# Progress Tracking

Every coordinator skill (`-all` suffix, plus `dx-req`, `dx-step`, `dx-simple`)
reports progress through a **progress file** in the spec directory. The file is
the single source of truth. Task-tracking tools are an optional display layer
that may not exist.

## Why a file, not a tool

Claude Code stopped offering `TaskCreate` / `TaskGet` / `TaskUpdate` /
`TaskList` / `TodoWrite` by default on Opus 4.8, Sonnet 5, Fable 5, Mythos 5
and newer models (v2.1.233; narrowed again in v2.1.260 — they now ship only on
Claude 3.x, Opus 4.0–4.7, Sonnet 4.0–4.6 and Haiku 4.5). Anthropic's reasoning:
newer models track multi-step work without a written checklist, and the tool
definitions cost context. They are opt-in from there on.

Those tools also never existed on Copilot CLI, Codex CLI or Gemini CLI, and
they are invisible in an ADO pipeline log, where no human watches a transcript.
A file survives every one of those cases, plus `/clear`, compaction and a
crashed run.

## Rules

- **The progress file is mandatory; the task tools are not.** Write the file
  first, every phase transition. Never make a phase transition conditional on a
  task tool being present.
- **Write it with the shared script**, so every skill produces the same table:
  ```bash
  DX_PROGRESS_FILE="dev-all-progress.md" DX_PROGRESS_TITLE="/dx-agent-all Progress" \
    bash .ai/lib/update-progress.sh "$SPEC_DIR" "Planning" "in_progress"
  ```
  Status values: `pending` · `in_progress` · `done` · `failed` · `skipped` ·
  `blocked`. One row per phase, updated in place — never append a second row
  for the same phase.

  The script path is project-relative on purpose: `/dx-init` installs the script
  to `.ai/lib/`, and `$CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT` is set only by Claude Code — it is
  unset on Copilot CLI, Codex CLI and Gemini CLI, and in the ADO pipeline agents.
- **Mirror into task tools only when they exist.** If `TaskCreate` is in the
  session's tool list, mirror the same phases so the user gets a live checklist.
  If it is absent, say nothing about it and carry on — a missing tool is the
  normal case, not a degraded one.
- **Top-level only.** Only the outermost coordinator mirrors into tasks.
  Subagents and forked skills (`context: fork`) write the progress file and
  never create their own task tree — a forked skill's task list is invisible to
  its parent anyway.
- **One progress file per skill invocation.** If a coordinator delegates to
  another coordinator (`dx-agent-all` → `dx-step-all`), the inner skill writes
  rows into the outer skill's file rather than starting its own.
- **Reference, do not quote.** Point at the progress file in chat and emit a
  one-line summary derived from it. Re-printing the whole table on each phase
  re-anchors it in context and doubles the cost of every recap.
- **Skipped phases** get a `skipped` row, not a deleted one. The file is a run
  record; a reader needs to see that a phase was considered and dropped.
- **Retries** update the note column (`retry 1`, `fix 2`, `healing`), not the
  phase name — otherwise the row is duplicated.

## Re-enabling the task tools (opt-in)

If a project wants the live checklist back on newer models, any one of these
opts the session in — no skill change needed:

| Where | How |
|---|---|
| Shell | `export CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_TODO_TOOLS=1` |
| Project | name `TaskCreate` in `.claude/settings.json` permissions allow list |
| One session | `claude --allowedTools TaskCreate` |
| ADO pipeline | add `TaskCreate,TaskUpdate,TaskList` to `ALLOWED_TOOLS` |
| Agent SDK | `allowedTools` / `tools` / `env` option (TypeScript `env` replaces the subprocess environment — spread `...process.env`) |

This is a display preference. It must never become a requirement for a skill to
complete.
